!tests/engine/world.ts
# The re-included file exists because `next build` type-checks scripts/backtest.ts,
# which imports its clock helpers and World type from tests/engine/world — the
# container build failed on its absence while every local and CI build passed.
#
# Do NOT add a bare `tests` line back above this. Docker cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory has already been excluded, so the two together
# silently cancel this out and the image build fails on the missing module
# again. Excluding the individual test directories works; excluding `tests` does
# not. Nothing here changes the shipped image: the final stage copies only
# .next/standalone, so no test source reaches the container.
coverage
